What is Comparator?

Comparator is an interface used to define custom ordering of objects.

Unlike Comparable,

Comparable → Defines one default (natural) ordering
Comparator → Defines multiple custom orderings

It belongs to

java.util.Comparator

Method

int compare(T o1, T o2);
Why was Comparator introduced?

Suppose we have

class Student{

    int id;
    String name;
    int marks;
    int age;

}

Now think...

How can students be sorted?

By ID

By Name

By Marks

By Age

By Roll Number

By Percentage

There are many possibilities.

Comparable allows only ONE natural ordering.

What if tomorrow the client says

"Earlier sort by ID.

Now sort by Name.

Next sort by Marks."

Should we keep changing compareTo() every time?

No.

That's why Java introduced Comparator.

Problem with Comparable

Suppose

class Student implements Comparable<Student>{

    int id;
    String name;
    int marks;

    @Override
    public int compareTo(Student other){

        return Integer.compare(this.id,other.id);

    }
}

