101

102

103

Tomorrow requirement changes.

Sort by Name

You modify

compareTo()

Again requirement changes.

Sort by Marks

Again modify compareTo().

This is not a good design.

One class should not be modified every time the sorting rule changes.

Comparator solves this.

Comparator Idea

Instead of putting comparison logic inside Student, put it in separate classes.

Example

Student

No sorting logic

Create

IdComparator

NameComparator

MarksComparator

AgeComparator

Each class knows only one sorting rule.

Student class remains unchanged.

This follows the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP).